      "summary": "Fix ASIO init crash on drivers with non-ASCII paths (#1648)",
      "description": "BassAsioDriver.Initialize() read the driver's file path via\nAsioDeviceInfo.Driver, which under Mono can throw\nExecutionEngineException: Illegal byte sequence when that path\ncontains non-ASCII bytes (e.g. RODE's driver installs under a path\ncontaining \"ø\"). The exception went uncaught, aborting ASIO\ninitialization entirely instead of just losing one piece of display\nmetadata.\n\nWrap the read in try/catch and fall back to the already-safe\nDriverName for DriverId on failure."
